/Title (wellness market. The example business problem is to estimate which customers are likely to purchase a product or service within a defined future period. Such a prediction can help a brand prioritise relevant offers, plan campaigns, improve customer engagement, and use marketing budgets more efficiently. The framework covers data preparation, validation, classification metrics, threshold selection, error analysis, model monitoring, and communication of results to business stakeholders.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 727 0 R
/Prev 783 0 R
/Next 818 0 R
>>
endobj
818 0 obj
<<
/Title (The evaluation does not rely on accuracy alone. Precision, recall, F1-score, and AUC-ROC are considered because customer purchase data may be imbalanced and because false positive and false negative predictions have different business costs. The report also explains how model scores should be translated into campaign decisions, while protecting customer privacy and avoiding unfair or misleading targeting.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 727 0 R
/Prev 817 0 R
/Next 784 0 R
>>
endobj
